{
  "score": 52,
  "score_rationale": "Nokia carries moderate risk: a conservative balance sheet and diversified telecom infrastructure exposure offset by structurally thin operating margins, significant earnings volatility, a stock trading ~56% above DCF intrinsic value, and meaningful competitive/macro headwinds in the 5G capex cycle.",
  "key_findings": [
    {
      "finding": "Operating margins are thin and highly volatile, swinging from -1.1% (Q1 prior year) to +9.7% within eight quarters, indicating fragile earnings quality and heavy seasonality risk.",
